---
scope: "The SVG is the source of truth for screen COMPOSITION on the `colonial_console`/CIC shell — for ART ([DEC-COLONIAL-OS-SVG-IS-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH]), for the render's LAYER Z-ORDER, for its LIVE-SLOT positions, and for TEXT STYLING ([DEC-SVG-COMPOSITION-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH], [DEC-CXC-COMP-SLOT-DELIMITER-AT]). One contract over a THREE-LAYER shell: (L1) a single authoritative BASE common SVG (`colonial_base_ux.svg` -> `bus://assets/cic/base.svg`) — the amber master-mask frame + `slot:radio@mode` + the status/firmware area + the shared row-1 controls + the shared confirmation dialog — composited UNDER every mode; (L2) a MODE SURFACE per radio mode (STD/DRADIS/EXT/CHRONO), each a SELF-CONTAINED surface owning its OWN navigation + content (STD's two-level tab nav lives IN STD, not in global chrome); (L3) per-(console, sub-tab) STD screens resolved BY REFERENCE, each a static BACKDROP + named live SLOTS. Facets: (1) LAYER-ORDER DERIVATION — Python introspects an `.svg`, sorts its top-level groups into THREE categories (rendered content/backdrop, `slot:` live widget, `ref:` ignored) and derives the canonical render z-order from the SVG's OWN group document order into a manifest the render picks up automatically, eliminating the hand-maintained code z-order that caused the EXT screen-area inversion; (2) the live-SLOT binding contract — a group whose label begins `slot:` is a binding point (`slot:<widget>@<binding>`, `@` delimiter) into which the render layers a reusable, bus-bound widget, its styling read from the slot's INNER SVG elements, its widget KIND naming the interaction/behavior (not the appearance); and (3) TEXT STYLING derived from each SVG `<text>` element. The SVG is the layout FRONT-END; the render LOWERS it; composition is intrinsic to the source, never re-specified in code ([DX-NARROW-WAIST])."
audience: [David (architect) — ratify the deepened mode-surface model (all design decisions now SETTLED), "the builder implementing the layer-order derivation + the slot router", the render-engineer maintaining the colonial_console shell, any screen author mocking a mode or a (console, sub-tab) in Inkscape, any Intelligence inspecting/swapping a screen, a mode surface, the base, or a composition manifest as a bus artifact]
boundary: "IN: the SVG-as-composition-source principle ([CXC-COMP-CREDO]); the three-layer shell model — the authoritative BASE common SVG ([CXC-COMP-BASE]), the self-contained MODE SURFACES that own their own nav ([CXC-COMP-MODE-SURFACE]), and the `ref:`/skip authoring convention + the derivation's THREE group categories ([CXC-COMP-REF]); the layer-order derivation from SVG group z-order ([CXC-COMP-LAYER-ORDER]) + the change/context_for_change that falsifies hand-maintained code z-order; the composition-manifest artifact format ([CXC-COMP-MANIFEST]); live-widget/art interleave by SVG z-position ([CXC-COMP-INTERLEAVE]); the STD per-(console, sub-tab) by-reference content contract ([CXC-COMP-STD-CONTENT]); the named live-SLOT binding convention with the `@` delimiter ([CXC-COMP-SLOT]); slot + chrome TEXT styling read from the inner SVG elements ([CXC-COMP-TEXT-STYLE]); the widget-KIND-names-behavior discipline ([CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]); the three screen KINDS ([CXC-COMP-KINDS]); missing-art -> placeholder + the base-shared/mode-owned split, where ownership is decided by element LOCATION with NO override mechanism ([CXC-COMP-MISSING], [DD-COMP-OWNERSHIP]); the machine+glass acceptance gates ([CXC-COMP-VERIFY]); and the hand-maintained->derived migration note ([CXC-COMP-LAYER-ORDER]). OUT: the CIC shell layer STACK definition + frame-as-master-mask ([CXC-CIC-WIDGET], reused not respec'd); the two-level nav + the row1 radio-mode content-source model ([CXC-CIC-NAV] / [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE], EXTENDED by reference — this doc deepens them into the mode-surface + STD-screen model); the Inkscape element-name -> scene-element mapping vocabulary + the artwork-kinds + the re-scan tool ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP] / [CXC-CIC-SVG-TABLE], reused as the derivation's input contract); the bus-asset resolve model + the baker (`bus://assets/...`, reused); the reusable widget implementations a slot binds (GaugeWidget/segmented_tab_row/graph/table/value — defined in the render-engine + widget-primitives specs, positioned here, not defined here). all design decisions are SETTLED: spec home, manifest format, slot grammar (`@` delimiter), and migration scope ([DEC-CXC-COMP-DDS-SETTLED], [DEC-CXC-COMP-SLOT-DELIMITER-AT]); and the base-vs-mode ownership rule — location decides ownership, no override — with the status/firmware area settled base-shared ([DD-COMP-OWNERSHIP], David 2026-08-04)."
not-this: "Not a new render engine or a new compositing path — the layer stack is still the `pixel_stack` + the opaque-overlay/transparent-window master mask ([CXC-CIC-WIDGET], [CXC-R-SPRITE-CONTAINER]); this doc changes WHERE composition comes from (the SVG, derived) not HOW layers composite. Not a new scan tool — it EXTENDS the existing deterministic SVG scan/bake ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]) with a three-category sort + a layer-order/slot-position/text-style derivation pass. Not a widget catalogue — the reusable widgets a slot binds are defined elsewhere and reused by reference. Not a CIC-shell respec — [SPEC:CXC-CIC] stands; this is its composition-source deepening. Not a hand-authored composition file — the manifest is DERIVED from the SVG and never hand-edited; a layer-inversion or masking problem is fixed in the `.svg`, not in code (David 2026-08-04). Not global chrome that owns the tab rows — the tab rows are STD's, owned by the STD mode surface, not shared chrome (this SUPERSEDES the earlier tabs-are-shared-chrome language; see [CXC-COMP-MODE-SURFACE])."
