**Updated**: 2026-08-04 (v0.3) — ADDED the lint-contract facet [CXC-COMP-LINT] (the SVG/composition linter as the authoritative conformance check) + its acceptance row COMP-C13. The linter IS the composition derivation ([CXC-COMP-LAYER-ORDER] + the three-category sort) run in `--check`/report mode, so lint == the render contract BY CONSTRUCTION (no second rule copy to drift). It enforces slot grammar / `ref:` usage / required-labels-present (turning the current opaque `radio-button-group-bounding-box`-absent chrome-bake CRASH into a readable "missing required label X" diagnostic) / no duplicate-or-dangling bindings / unregistered-kind ERROR / unmapped-group WARNING / layer-z sanity. Runs as ONE linter, N front-ends: the bake/publish pipeline REFUSES on lint failure (fail-loud), plus CLI (`lint <svg>`), CI, and an Intelligence bus peer; an optional later THIN Inkscape extension shells out to the standalone linter (front-end only, never a fork). A `change`/`context_for_change` block records the supersession of the no-gate/opaque-crash bake behavior; the node is flagged `build-basis` for the follow-on ENGINE build slice (derivation-in-check-mode, after the derivation it reuses). Edges declared: [CXC-COMP-LINT] USES [CXC-COMP-LAYER-ORDER]; DEPENDS_ON [CXC-COMP-REF]/[CXC-COMP-SLOT]/[CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]/[CXC-COMP-BASE]; RELATED_TO [CXC-COMP-MANIFEST]/[CXC-COMP-VERIFY]; UPHOLDS [CXC-COMP-CREDO]; REALIZES [DEC-SVG-COMPOSITION-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH].
**Updated**: 2026-08-04 (v0.2) — deepened from the initial draft into the FULL CIC composition model David and the architect converged on. ADDED the three-layer shell: [CXC-COMP-BASE] (the one authoritative base common SVG composited under every mode), [CXC-COMP-MODE-SURFACE] (each mode a self-contained surface owning its own nav — STD's tab rows are STD's, not shared chrome), and [CXC-COMP-REF] (the `ref:` ignore convention + the derivation's three group categories: rendered / `slot:` / `ref:`). ADDED [CXC-COMP-TEXT-STYLE] (slot + chrome styling read from the inner `<text>`/shape, set on `<text>` not `<tspan>`) and [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND] (a widget kind names interaction/behavior, not appearance). REVISED [CXC-COMP-SLOT] + [DD-COMP-SLOT-NAMING] from the first-hyphen split to `slot:<widget>@<binding>` (the `@` delimiter, hyphen-safe) per [DEC-CXC-COMP-SLOT-DELIMITER-AT]. REVISED [CXC-COMP-MISSING] from a shared `chrome.svg` that owned the tab rows to the base-shared / mode-owned split. SETTLED the base-vs-mode ownership rule as [DD-COMP-OWNERSHIP] (ownership by element LOCATION, NO override mechanism; status/firmware area base-shared) — folding David's 2026-08-04 resolution and REMOVING the former open DD-COMP-STATUS-BAR-OVERRIDE (status-bar-override) node. change/context_for_change blocks record the two supersessions (first-hyphen -> `@` on [CXC-COMP-SLOT]/[DD-COMP-SLOT-NAMING]; tabs-are-shared-chrome -> mode-owned on [CXC-COMP-MODE-SURFACE]/[CXC-COMP-MISSING]), plus the retained hand-maintained -> derived block on [CXC-COMP-LAYER-ORDER].
**Status**: RATIFY-READY (deepened model — ALL design decisions SETTLED, no open sub-items). SETTLED: [DD-COMP-SPEC-HOME] = this 53- doc; [DD-COMP-MANIFEST-FORMAT] = derived JSON sidecar; [DD-COMP-SLOT-NAMING] = `slot:<widget>@<binding>` (`@` delimiter, [DEC-CXC-COMP-SLOT-DELIMITER-AT]); [DD-COMP-MIGRATION-SCOPE] = CIC-shell-only; [DD-COMP-OWNERSHIP] = ownership by element LOCATION, NO override mechanism (base SVG = shared, mode SVG = mode-owned), with the status/firmware area settled BASE-SHARED (David 2026-08-04 — resolving the former status-bar open call: not override-capable; if a mode ever needs a status line it is authored in the mode SVG, not overridden). NEXT: architect ratifies the deepened model, then the composition-derivation + slot-router build (render-engineer), including moving the tab rows under STD so the tabs-in-EXT problem is designed out.
